/-!
# Every algebra is a direct limit of algebras of finite presentation

Proof of Stacks 00QN: for a ring map `R → A` there is a directed partially ordered set `Λ` and a
directed system `(A_l)_{l ∈ Λ}` of `R`-algebras of finite presentation with `A = colim_l A_l`, and
if `A` is of finite type over `R` the system may be chosen with surjective transition maps.

This is the source's second proof. Inside the polynomial ring `P = R[X_a ; a ∈ A]` on the
underlying set of `A`, with `ev : P → A` the evaluation `X_a ↦ a`, a finite subset `S ⊆ A` and a
finite set `E ⊆ P` of polynomials determine the finitely presented `R`-algebra
`A_{S, E} = R[X_s ; s ∈ S] / (E ∩ ker ev)`, together with the map `A_{S, E} → A` induced by `ev`;
enlarging `S` and `E` gives the transition maps. The image of `A_{S, E} → A` is the subalgebra of
`A` generated by `S`, so every `a ∈ A` is hit already by `A_{{a}, ∅} = R[X_a]`, and an element of
`A_{S, E}` represented by `p` and dying in `A` dies already in `A_{S, E ∪ {p}}`; hence the induced
map from the colimit is bijective. If `↑σ` generates `A` as an `R`-algebra one keeps `S = σ` fixed
and lets only `E` grow: the transition maps are then quotient maps of the fixed algebra
`R[X_s ; s ∈ σ]`, hence surjective, and `R[X_s ; s ∈ σ]` already surjects onto `A`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.DirectLimit.AlgebraApproximation.solution`: the statement of Tag 00QN.

## Implementation notes

The two systems of the source are built from one set of primitives, parametrized by a pair `(S, E)`
of a finite subset of `A` and a finite set of polynomials:
`Stacks.DirectLimit.AlgebraApproximation.Quo`, its transition maps
`Stacks.DirectLimit.AlgebraApproximation.trans` and its map
`Stacks.DirectLimit.AlgebraApproximation.toA` to `A`. The two facts about them that carry the proof
are `Stacks.DirectLimit.AlgebraApproximation.range_evOn`, computing the image of
`R[X_s ; s ∈ S] → A` as the subalgebra generated by `S`, and
`Stacks.DirectLimit.AlgebraApproximation.bijective_lift`, which proves `A = colim` for any index
type mapping monotonically to such pairs, given that every element of `A` lies in the subalgebra
generated by some `S` and that every relation can be adjoined.
`Stacks.DirectLimit.AlgebraApproximation.exists_system_of` packages such an index type into the
existential asserted by Tag 00QN, with surjectivity of the transition maps asserted only under an
arbitrary hypothesis `Q`; both sentences of the source are instantiations of it with `Q` the finite
type assumption, the first for `Λ = Finset A × Finset P` in the case where that assumption is
refuted, the second for `Λ = Finset P` with `S` frozen in the case where it holds.

The algebras `R[X_s ; s ∈ S]` are realized as the subalgebras `MvPolynomial.supported R ↑S` of the
single ring `P`, rather than as `MvPolynomial ↥S R`, so that the relations of every index live in
one and the same ring and the index set carries no dependent types. Since only the elements of `E`
lying in `R[X_s ; s ∈ S]` and in `ker ev` are used as relations, no compatibility condition
between `S` and `E` has to be imposed, and the index set is a plain product with the product order.

## References

* [StacksProject 00QN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00QN)
-/

namespace Stacks.DirectLimit.AlgebraApproximation


open MvPolynomial

variable (R : Type u) [CommRing R] (A : Type v) [CommRing A] [Algebra R A]

/-- The polynomial ring over `R` on the underlying set of `A`. -/
private abbrev Pol : Type max u v := MvPolynomial A R

/-- Evaluation `R[X_a ; a ∈ A] → A`, `X_a ↦ a`. -/
private noncomputable abbrev ev : Pol R A →ₐ[R] A := aeval (id : A → A)

/-- The subalgebra of polynomials supported on the finite subset `S` of `A`. -/
private abbrev Sub (S : Finset A) : Type max u v := ↥(supported R (↑S : Set A))

/-- Evaluation restricted to polynomials supported on `S`. -/
private noncomputable abbrev evOn (S : Finset A) : Sub R A S →ₐ[R] A :=
  (ev R A).comp (Subalgebra.val _)

/-- The image of `R[X_s ; s ∈ S] → A` is the `R`-subalgebra of `A` generated by `S`. -/
private theorem range_evOn (S : Finset A) :
    (evOn R A S).range = Algebra.adjoin R (↑S : Set A) := by
  rw [Subalgebra.range_comp_val, supported_eq_adjoin_X, ← Algebra.adjoin_image, ← Set.image_comp]
  simp

omit [CommRing A] [Algebra R A] in
private theorem finitePresentation_sub (S : Finset A) :
    Algebra.FinitePresentation R (Sub R A S) :=
  have : Algebra.FinitePresentation R (MvPolynomial (↑S : Set A) R) :=
    Algebra.FinitePresentation.mvPolynomial R R _
  Algebra.FinitePresentation.equiv (supportedEquivMvPolynomial (↑S : Set A)).symm

/-- The ideal of relations selected by `E`: the ideal of `R[X_s ; s ∈ S]` generated by those
elements of `E` which are supported on `S` and vanish at `X_a ↦ a`. -/
private noncomputable def rel (S : Finset A) (E : Finset (Pol R A)) : Ideal (Sub R A S) :=
  Ideal.span {x : Sub R A S | (x : Pol R A) ∈ E ∧ evOn R A S x = 0}

/-- The algebra `A_{S, E} = R[X_s ; s ∈ S] / (E)` of the source. -/
private abbrev Quo (S : Finset A) (E : Finset (Pol R A)) : Type max u v :=
  Sub R A S ⧸ rel R A S E

private theorem mem_rel {S : Finset A} {E : Finset (Pol R A)} (x : Sub R A S)
    (hxE : (x : Pol R A) ∈ E) (hx0 : evOn R A S x = 0) : x ∈ rel R A S E :=
  Ideal.subset_span ⟨hxE, hx0⟩

private theorem rel_le {S : Finset A} {E : Finset (Pol R A)} {I : Ideal (Sub R A S)}
    (h : ∀ x : Sub R A S, (x : Pol R A) ∈ E → evOn R A S x = 0 → x ∈ I) : rel R A S E ≤ I := by
  rw [rel, Ideal.span_le]
  rintro x ⟨hxE, hx0⟩
  exact h x hxE hx0

private theorem rel_fg (S : Finset A) (E : Finset (Pol R A)) : (rel R A S E).FG :=
  Submodule.fg_span <|
    (E.finite_toSet.preimage Subtype.val_injective.injOn).subset fun _ hx => hx.1

private theorem finitePresentation_quo (S : Finset A) (E : Finset (Pol R A)) :
    Algebra.FinitePresentation R (Quo R A S E) :=
  have := finitePresentation_sub R A S
  Algebra.FinitePresentation.quotient (rel_fg R A S E)

/-- The inclusion `R[X_s ; s ∈ S] → R[X_s ; s ∈ S']` for `S ⊆ S'`. -/
private noncomputable def incl {S S' : Finset A} (h : S ≤ S') : Sub R A S →ₐ[R] Sub R A S' :=
  Subalgebra.inclusion (supported_mono (Finset.coe_subset.mpr h))

omit [CommRing A] [Algebra R A] in
private theorem coe_incl {S S' : Finset A} (h : S ≤ S') (x : Sub R A S) :
    ((incl R A h x : Sub R A S') : Pol R A) = (x : Pol R A) :=
  Subalgebra.coe_inclusion _ x

omit [CommRing A] [Algebra R A] in
private theorem incl_self {S : Finset A} (h : S ≤ S) (x : Sub R A S) : incl R A h x = x :=
  Subtype.ext (coe_incl R A h x)

omit [CommRing A] [Algebra R A] in
private theorem incl_incl {S₁ S₂ S₃ : Finset A} (h₁ : S₁ ≤ S₂) (h₂ : S₂ ≤ S₃) (x : Sub R A S₁) :
    incl R A h₂ (incl R A h₁ x) = incl R A (h₁.trans h₂) x :=
  Subtype.ext (by rw [coe_incl, coe_incl, coe_incl])

private theorem evOn_incl {S S' : Finset A} (h : S ≤ S') (x : Sub R A S) :
    evOn R A S' (incl R A h x) = evOn R A S x := by
  change ev R A ((incl R A h x : Sub R A S') : Pol R A) = ev R A (x : Pol R A)
  rw [coe_incl]

/-- A polynomial supported on `S` which lies in `E'` and vanishes at `X_a ↦ a` is a relation of
`A_{S', E'}`, for every `S' ⊇ S`. -/
private theorem incl_mem_rel {S S' : Finset A} {E' : Finset (Pol R A)} (hS : S ≤ S')
    (x : Sub R A S) (hxE : (x : Pol R A) ∈ E') (hx0 : evOn R A S x = 0) :
    incl R A hS x ∈ rel R A S' E' :=
  mem_rel R A _ (by rw [coe_incl]; exact hxE) (by rw [evOn_incl]; exact hx0)

private theorem rel_le_comap {S S' : Finset A} {E E' : Finset (Pol R A)} (hS : S ≤ S')
    (hE : E ≤ E') : rel R A S E ≤ Ideal.comap (incl R A hS) (rel R A S' E') :=
  rel_le R A fun x hxE hx0 => Ideal.mem_comap.mpr (incl_mem_rel R A hS x (hE hxE) hx0)

/-- The transition map `A_{S, E} → A_{S', E'}` for `S ⊆ S'` and `E ⊆ E'`. -/
private noncomputable def trans {S S' : Finset A} {E E' : Finset (Pol R A)} (hS : S ≤ S')
    (hE : E ≤ E') : Quo R A S E →ₐ[R] Quo R A S' E' :=
  Ideal.quotientMapₐ _ (incl R A hS) (rel_le_comap R A hS hE)

private theorem trans_mk {S S' : Finset A} {E E' : Finset (Pol R A)} (hS : S ≤ S') (hE : E ≤ E')
    (x : Sub R A S) : trans R A hS hE (Ideal.Quotient.mk (rel R A S E) x)
      = Ideal.Quotient.mk (rel R A S' E') (incl R A hS x) := rfl

private theorem trans_self {S : Finset A} {E : Finset (Pol R A)} (hS : S ≤ S) (hE : E ≤ E)
    (x : Quo R A S E) : trans R A hS hE x = x := by
  obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective x
  rw [trans_mk, incl_self]

private theorem trans_trans {S₁ S₂ S₃ : Finset A} {E₁ E₂ E₃ : Finset (Pol R A)}
    (h₁ : S₁ ≤ S₂) (h₂ : S₂ ≤ S₃) (k₁ : E₁ ≤ E₂) (k₂ : E₂ ≤ E₃) (x : Quo R A S₁ E₁) :
    trans R A h₂ k₂ (trans R A h₁ k₁ x) = trans R A (h₁.trans h₂) (k₁.trans k₂) x := by
  obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective x
  rw [trans_mk, trans_mk, trans_mk, incl_incl]

private theorem trans_surjective {S : Finset A} {E E' : Finset (Pol R A)} (hS : S ≤ S)
    (hE : E ≤ E') : Function.Surjective (trans R A hS hE) := by
  intro y
  obtain ⟨b, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective y
  exact ⟨Ideal.Quotient.mk _ b, by rw [trans_mk, incl_self]⟩

/-- Adjoining a relation kills it: an element of `A_{S, E}` represented by a polynomial `p` that
vanishes at `X_a ↦ a` dies in `A_{S', E'}` as soon as `p ∈ E'`. -/
private theorem trans_mk_eq_zero {S S' : Finset A} {E E' : Finset (Pol R A)} (hS : S ≤ S')
    (hE : E ≤ E') (x : Sub R A S) (hxE : (x : Pol R A) ∈ E') (hx0 : evOn R A S x = 0) :
    trans R A hS hE (Ideal.Quotient.mk (rel R A S E) x) = 0 := by
  rw [trans_mk, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem]
  exact incl_mem_rel R A hS x hxE hx0

private theorem evOn_eq_zero_of_mem_rel {S : Finset A} {E : Finset (Pol R A)} {x : Sub R A S}
    (hx : x ∈ rel R A S E) : evOn R A S x = 0 :=
  rel_le R A (I := RingHom.ker (evOn R A S).toRingHom) (fun _ _ h => h) hx

/-- The canonical map `A_{S, E} → A`. -/
private noncomputable def toA (S : Finset A) (E : Finset (Pol R A)) : Quo R A S E →ₐ[R] A :=
  Ideal.Quotient.liftₐ _ (evOn R A S) fun _ hx => evOn_eq_zero_of_mem_rel R A hx

private theorem toA_mk (S : Finset A) (E : Finset (Pol R A)) (x : Sub R A S) :
    toA R A S E (Ideal.Quotient.mk (rel R A S E) x) = evOn R A S x := rfl

private theorem toA_trans {S S' : Finset A} {E E' : Finset (Pol R A)} (hS : S ≤ S') (hE : E ≤ E')
    (x : Quo R A S E) : toA R A S' E' (trans R A hS hE x) = toA R A S E x := by
  obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective x
  rw [trans_mk, toA_mk, toA_mk, evOn_incl]

section System

-- `Pol R A` is spelled out here: a `private` declaration named in a `variable` command
-- elaborates to a `sorryAx` placeholder, poisoning every declaration that uses the variable.
variable {Λ : Type max u v} [PartialOrder Λ] {Sf : Λ → Finset A}
  {Ef : Λ → Finset (MvPolynomial A R)}

private theorem directedSystem_trans (hSf : Monotone Sf) (hEf : Monotone Ef) :
    DirectedSystem (fun l => Quo R A (Sf l) (Ef l))
      (fun _i _j h => ⇑(trans R A (hSf h) (hEf h))) :=
  { map_self := fun _ x => trans_self R A _ _ x
    map_map := fun _ _ _ _ _ x => trans_trans R A _ _ _ _ x }

/-- **`A` is the colimit.** If every element of `A` lies in the subalgebra of `A` generated by
some `Sf l`, and every polynomial supported on `Sf l` and vanishing at `X_a ↦ a` lies in `Ef l'`
for some `l' ≥ l`, then `colim_l A_{Sf l, Ef l} → A` is bijective. -/
private theorem bijective_lift [Nonempty Λ] [IsDirectedOrder Λ] (hSf : Monotone Sf)
    (hEf : Monotone Ef)
    (hds : DirectedSystem (fun l => Quo R A (Sf l) (Ef l))
      (fun _i _j h => ⇑(trans R A (hSf h) (hEf h))))
    (hmem : ∀ a : A, ∃ l, a ∈ Algebra.adjoin R (↑(Sf l) : Set A))
    (hker : ∀ (l : Λ) (x : Sub R A (Sf l)), evOn R A (Sf l) x = 0 →
      ∃ l' ≥ l, (x : Pol R A) ∈ Ef l') :
    Function.Bijective (DirectLimit.Algebra.lift (fun l => Quo R A (Sf l) (Ef l))
      (fun _i _j h => trans R A (hSf h) (hEf h)) A (fun l => toA R A (Sf l) (Ef l))
      (fun _i _j h x => toA_trans R A (hSf h) (hEf h) x)) := by
  refine ⟨(injective_iff_map_eq_zero _).2 fun z hz => ?_, fun a => ?_⟩
  · obtain ⟨l, x, rfl⟩ := DirectLimit.exists_eq_mk _ z
    obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective x
    have h0 : evOn R A (Sf l) y = 0 := hz
    obtain ⟨l', hll', hy⟩ := hker l y h0
    rw [DirectLimit.exists_eq_zero]
    exact ⟨l', hll', trans_mk_eq_zero R A (hSf hll') (hEf hll') y hy h0⟩
  · obtain ⟨l, hl⟩ := hmem a
    obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := (evOn R A (Sf l)).mem_range.mp ((range_evOn R A (Sf l)).ge hl)
    exact ⟨⟦⟨l, Ideal.Quotient.mk _ x⟩⟧, hx⟩

/-- The system indexed by `Λ`, packaged as the existential asserted by Tag 00QN. Surjectivity of
the transition maps is asserted under an arbitrary hypothesis `Q`, so that one packaging serves
both the general system, where `Q` is refuted, and the system with `S` frozen, whose transition
maps are surjective outright. -/
private theorem exists_system_of [Nonempty Λ] [IsDirectedOrder Λ] {Q : Prop}
    (hSf : Monotone Sf) (hEf : Monotone Ef)
    (hmem : ∀ a : A, ∃ l, a ∈ Algebra.adjoin R (↑(Sf l) : Set A))
    (hker : ∀ (l : Λ) (x : Sub R A (Sf l)), evOn R A (Sf l) x = 0 →
      ∃ l' ≥ l, (x : Pol R A) ∈ Ef l')
    (hsurj : Q → ∀ (i j : Λ) (h : i ≤ j), Function.Surjective (trans R A (hSf h) (hEf h))) :
    ∃ (Λ' : Type (max u v)) (_ : PartialOrder Λ') (_ : Nonempty Λ') (_ : IsDirectedOrder Λ')
      (G : Λ' → Type (max u v)) (_ : ∀ l, CommRing (G l)) (_ : ∀ l, Algebra R (G l))
      (f : ∀ i j, i ≤ j → G i →ₐ[R] G j) (_ : DirectedSystem G fun i j h ↦ ⇑(f i j h))
      (g : ∀ l, G l →ₐ[R] A) (hg : ∀ i j h x, g j (f i j h x) = g i x),
      (∀ l, Algebra.FinitePresentation R (G l)) ∧
      (Q → ∀ i j (h : i ≤ j), Function.Surjective (f i j h)) ∧
      Function.Bijective (DirectLimit.Algebra.lift G f A g hg) :=
  ⟨Λ, ‹PartialOrder Λ›, ‹Nonempty Λ›, ‹IsDirectedOrder Λ›, fun l => Quo R A (Sf l) (Ef l),
    fun _ => inferInstance, fun _ => inferInstance, fun _i _j h => trans R A (hSf h) (hEf h),
    directedSystem_trans R A hSf hEf, fun l => toA R A (Sf l) (Ef l),
    fun _i _j h x => toA_trans R A (hSf h) (hEf h) x,
    fun l => finitePresentation_quo R A (Sf l) (Ef l), hsurj,
    bijective_lift R A hSf hEf (directedSystem_trans R A hSf hEf) hmem hker⟩

end System

/-- **Every algebra is a direct limit of algebras of finite presentation.** -/
public theorem solution :
    ∃ (Λ : Type (max u v)) (_ : PartialOrder Λ) (_ : Nonempty Λ) (_ : IsDirectedOrder Λ)
      (G : Λ → Type (max u v)) (_ : ∀ l, CommRing (G l)) (_ : ∀ l, Algebra R (G l))
      (f : ∀ i j, i ≤ j → G i →ₐ[R] G j) (_ : DirectedSystem G fun i j h ↦ ⇑(f i j h))
      (g : ∀ l, G l →ₐ[R] A) (hg : ∀ i j h x, g j (f i j h x) = g i x),
      (∀ l, Algebra.FinitePresentation R (G l)) ∧
      (Algebra.FiniteType R A → ∀ i j (h : i ≤ j), Function.Surjective (f i j h)) ∧
      Function.Bijective (DirectLimit.Algebra.lift G f A g hg) := by
  classical
  by_cases hft : Algebra.FiniteType R A
  · -- `A` is generated by a finite set `σ`: freeze `S = σ` and let only `E` grow.
    obtain ⟨σ, hσ⟩ := hft.out
    exact exists_system_of R A (Sf := fun _ => σ) (Ef := id) monotone_const monotone_id
      (fun a => ⟨∅, hσ.ge Algebra.mem_top⟩)
      (fun E x _ => ⟨insert (x : Pol R A) E, Finset.subset_insert _ _, Finset.mem_insert_self _ _⟩)
      fun _ _ _ h => trans_surjective R A (monotone_const h) (monotone_id h)
  · -- In general let both `S` and `E` grow; `a ∈ A` is hit by `A_{{a}, ∅} = R[X_a]`.
    exact exists_system_of R A (Λ := Finset A × Finset (Pol R A)) monotone_fst monotone_snd
      (fun a => ⟨({a}, ∅), Algebra.subset_adjoin (by simp)⟩)
      (fun l x _ => ⟨(l.1, insert (x : Pol R A) l.2), ⟨le_rfl, Finset.subset_insert _ _⟩,
        Finset.mem_insert_self _ _⟩)
      fun h => absurd h hft

end Stacks.DirectLimit.AlgebraApproximation

/-!
# Every algebra is a direct limit of algebras of finite presentation

Let `R → A` be a ring map. Then `A` is the colimit of a directed system of `R`-algebras of
finite presentation: there is a directed partially ordered set `Λ`, a system of `R`-algebras
`G l` of finite presentation with transition maps `f i j : G i →ₐ[R] G j` for `i ≤ j`, and a
compatible family `g l : G l →ₐ[R] A` inducing an isomorphism `colim_l G l ≅ A`. Moreover, if
`A` is of finite type over `R`, the system can be chosen with all transition maps surjective.

Concretely, `Λ` is the set of pairs `(S, E)` with `S ⊆ A` finite and `E` a finite set of
polynomials in `R[X_s ; s ∈ S]` vanishing on the chosen elements, ordered by inclusion in both
coordinates, and `G (S, E) = R[X_s ; s ∈ S] / (E)`; when `A = R[x_1, …, x_n] / I` one restricts
to the pairs with `S = {x_1, …, x_n}`, where the transition maps are quotient maps and hence
surjective. Alternatively the statement follows from the fact that the category of finitely
presented `R`-algebras over `A` is filtered with colimit `A` (tag `0BUF`) together with the
comparison of filtered colimits and directed colimits (Categories, Lemma `0032`).

## Main results

* `Algebra.exists_directedSystem_finitePresentation_lift_bijective`: every `R`-algebra `A` is
  the direct limit of a directed system of `R`-algebras of finite presentation, and the system
  may be chosen with surjective transition maps as soon as `A` is of finite type over `R`.

## Implementation notes

The colimit is spelled with `DirectLimit`, Mathlib's direct limit of a directed system of
algebraic structures, and "`A` is that colimit" is `Function.Bijective` of
`DirectLimit.Algebra.lift G f A g hg`, the `R`-algebra map out of the direct limit induced by
the compatible family `g`. This pins the comparison map rather than merely asserting an
abstract isomorphism `colim_l G l ≃ₐ[R] A`: the structure maps `G l → A` are part of the data,
and `DirectLimit.Algebra.lift_of` identifies the composite `G l → colim → A` with `g l`.

The index set is required to be a `PartialOrder`, not just a `Preorder`, since the pairs
`(S, E)` above are ordered by inclusion; this is the source's "directed partially ordered set"
and is the same strengthening Mathlib makes in `CategoryTheory.IsFiltered.exists_directed`.

The two sentences of the source are one existential here, the second appearing as the
implication `Algebra.FiniteType R A → ∀ i j h, Function.Surjective (f i j h)` among the
properties of the system produced. This is equivalent to the conjunction of the two sentences —
it gives each of them, and conversely a system for each case can be selected by cases on
whether `A` is of finite type — while keeping a single directed system, so that a user in the
finite type case does not have to re-derive finite presentation for a second system.

`Λ` and the `G l` are placed in `Type (max u v)` for `R : Type u` and `A : Type v`: the algebras
`R[X_s ; s ∈ S] / (E)` are quotients of polynomial rings on subsets of `A` with coefficients in
`R`, so neither universe alone suffices, and a universe cannot be existentially quantified.

Faithfulness. (1) The only data are `R`, `A` and the algebra structure, all of which the
conclusion mentions; there is no hypothesis, the finite type assumption of the second sentence
being an implication inside the conclusion, where it is used. (2) The scalars and base are the
source's: `Λ`-indexed system, transition maps and comparison map are all `R`-algebra maps
(`→ₐ[R]`), and finite presentation is over `R`. (3) The canonical maps are pinned: the family
`g` is part of the existential and the bijectivity is of the induced map out of the colimit, so
the isomorphism is the comparison map, not an unrelated one. (4) The instantiation is not
degenerate: for `A = R[x_1, x_2, x_3, …]`, a polynomial ring on infinitely many variables, `A`
is not of finite presentation over `R`, so no one-object system can satisfy the conclusion and
the asserted directed system is genuinely infinite; and the surjectivity clause has content
already for `A = R[x_1, …, x_n] / I` with `I` not finitely generated, where the system is
indexed by the finitely generated subideals of `I`.

